// Figure 4.8 — State chart: a transaction record from receipt to storage
// Eraser: New diagram > Flow chart, paste this code.
direction right

Initial [shape: oval, color: black, label: ""]
Received [shape: rectangle, icon: inbox, color: gray]
Validated [shape: rectangle, icon: check, color: blue]
Rejected [shape: rectangle, icon: slash, color: red]
Scoring [shape: rectangle, icon: cpu, color: purple]
Scored low risk [shape: rectangle, icon: shield, color: green]
Scored high risk [shape: rectangle, icon: alert-triangle, color: red]
Scoring failed [shape: rectangle, icon: alert-octagon, color: orange]
Stored [shape: rectangle, icon: database, color: blue]
Final [shape: oval, color: black, label: ""]

Initial > Received: POST with API key
Received > Rejected: bad key / invalid fields / duplicate id
Received > Validated: matches the 30-feature contract
Validated > Scoring: threshold read, request sent
Scoring > Scored low risk: probability below threshold
Scoring > Scored high risk: probability ≥ threshold, raises alert
Scoring > Scoring failed: timeout or service down
Scored low risk > Stored
Scored high risk > Stored
Scoring failed > Stored: kept, never dropped
Stored > Final
Rejected > Final: nothing written
